01:08:24,133 --> 01:08:25,366
<b>empty stretch below it,</b>

235
01:08:25,666 --> 01:08:27,800
<b>because there was barely anything there.</b>

236
01:08:28,333 --> 01:08:29,666
<b>Hot, barren,</b>

237
01:08:29,966 --> 01:08:32,533
<b>half-invented, not an icecap.</b>

238
01:08:33,333 --> 01:08:34,566
<b>And Piri Reis wasn't</b>

239
01:08:34,566 --> 01:08:36,000
<b>the only map to do this.</b>

240
01:08:36,366 --> 01:08:37,233
<b>They all did.</b>

241
01:08:37,800 --> 01:08:38,966
<b>That's the giveaway.</b>

242
01:08:39,533 --> 01:08:41,166
<b>No two of them drew the southern</b>

243
01:08:41,166 --> 01:08:42,500
<b>continent the same way,</b>

244
01:08:42,633 --> 01:08:43,433
<b>because none of them</b>

245
01:08:43,433 --> 01:08:44,699
<b>had actually seen it.</b>

246
01:08:45,533 --> 01:08:48,100
<b>So the lost civilization writers kept a</b>

247
01:08:48,100 --> 01:08:49,699
<b>handful whose guesses happened to</b>

248
01:08:49,699 --> 01:08:50,966
<b>resemble Antarctica.</b>

249
01:08:51,766 --> 01:08:53,366
<b>Piri Reis among them, and</b>

250
01:08:53,399 --> 01:08:55,166
<b>ignored the dozens that didn't.</b>

251
01:08:55,766 --> 01:08:57,766
<b>Real maps of a real coast</b>

252
01:08:58,000 --> 01:08:59,233
<b>would agree with each other.</b>

253
01:08:59,833 --> 01:09:00,933
<b>These don't.</b>

254
01:09:01,433 --> 01:09:02,766
<b>That isn't evidence.</b>

255
01:09:02,933 --> 01:09:04,466
<b>It's shopping for it.</b>

256
01:09:05,100 --> 01:09:07,166
<b>This shape was never the real story.</b>

257
01:09:07,333 --> 01:09:09,166
<b>This map sat forgotten in a palace</b>

258
01:09:09,166 --> 01:09:11,366
<b>library for 400 years.</b>

259
01:09:11,666 --> 01:09:12,433
<b>Not hidden.</b>

260
01:09:12,766 --> 01:09:13,833
<b>Not suppressed.</b>

261
01:09:14,233 --> 01:09:15,566
<b>Just ignored.</b>

262
01:09:16,199 --> 01:09:17,266
<b>And being ignored is the</b>

263
01:09:17,300 --> 01:09:18,699
<b>only thing that saved it.</b>

264
01:09:19,000 --> 01:09:21,233
<b>Piri Reis was drawing this map for an</b>

265
01:09:21,233 --> 01:09:22,633
<b>empire whose government,</b>

266
01:09:23,033 --> 01:09:26,233
<b>the Porte, the Sultan, and his court had</b>

267
01:09:26,233 --> 01:09:27,666
<b>no use for what he did.</b>

268
01:09:28,666 --> 01:09:31,033
<b>In the same century, Spain and Portugal</b>

269
01:09:31,100 --> 01:09:32,699
<b>each ran a government office</b>

270
01:09:32,699 --> 01:09:35,100
<b>where each voyage's findings got added to</b>

271
01:09:35,100 --> 01:09:36,466
<b>a single master chart,</b>

272
01:09:36,766 --> 01:09:39,033
<b>kept up to date by paid cartographers.</b>

273
01:09:39,666 --> 01:09:41,033
<b>The Ottoman state had nothing</b>

274
01:09:41,033 --> 01:09:43,633
<b>like that, and didn't want it.</b>

275
01:09:44,133 --> 01:09:46,733
<b>As Swat Suzegh puts it, "Piri</b>

276
01:09:46,733 --> 01:09:48,866
<b>Reis's maps represented a world</b>

277
01:09:48,899 --> 01:09:49,866
<b>that lay beyond the</b>

278
01:09:49,866 --> 01:09:51,566
<b>horizon of the Porte's ambition."</b>

279
01:09:52,433 --> 01:09:54,633
<b>The map was rolled up and shelved.</b>

280
01:09:55,266 --> 01:09:58,933
<b>As for Piri Reis, around 1553, in his</b>

281
01:09:58,933 --> 01:10:01,133
<b>80s, he lost a sea battle.</b>

282
01:10:01,366 --> 01:10:03,466
<b>The governor of Egypt reported him to the</b>

283
01:10:03,466 --> 01:10:06,466
<b>Sultan, and Suleiman had him executed.</b>

284
01:10:06,766 --> 01:10:09,100
<b>He died never knowing that the map he'd</b>

285
01:10:09,166 --> 01:10:10,366
<b>drawn, the one that</b>

286
01:10:10,433 --> 01:10:11,833
<b>answered every question people</b>

287
01:10:11,866 --> 01:10:13,833
<b>spent the next five centuries asking.</b>

288
01:10:14,533 --> 01:10:16,866
<b>He died never knowing that the map he'd</b>

289
01:10:16,899 --> 01:10:18,166
<b>drawn was still</b>

290
01:10:18,166 --> 01:10:19,733
<b>sitting where he'd left it.</b>

291
01:10:20,566 --> 01:10:22,966
<b>Suzegh calls it, "A strange map,</b>

292
01:10:23,266 --> 01:10:25,366
<b>which was mutilated remainsly forgotten</b>

293
01:10:25,366 --> 01:10:27,466
<b>in the library of Tokapi Palace."</b>

294
01:10:28,033 --> 01:10:30,166
<b>That's where the man's story ends.</b>

295
01:10:30,399 --> 01:10:32,066
<b>The map was only beginning.</b>

296
01:10:33,066 --> 01:10:34,966
<b>And there it stayed, in a storeroom</b>

297
01:10:34,966 --> 01:10:35,833
<b>nobody had properly</b>

298
01:10:35,833 --> 01:10:37,600
<b>catalogued until 1929,</b>

299
01:10:38,166 --> 01:10:39,033
<b>when the palace was</b>

300
01:10:39,033 --> 01:10:40,633
<b>being turned into a museum,</b>

301
01:10:40,766 --> 01:10:42,166
<b>and the director found it.</b>

302
01:10:42,766 --> 01:10:46,433
<b>It reached Paul Kallem, who, by luck, had</b>

303
01:10:46,433 --> 01:10:47,600
<b>spent the previous years</b>

304
01:10:47,600 --> 01:10:49,066
<b>on Piri Reis' other book,</b>

305
01:10:49,333 --> 01:10:50,399
<b>the Sailing Manual.</b>

306
01:10:50,833 --> 01:10:52,800
<b>He knew the hand the moment he saw it,</b>

307
01:10:53,033 --> 01:10:54,366
<b>and he caught what no</b>

308
01:10:54,366 --> 01:10:56,133
<b>one had in four centuries.</b>

309
01:10:56,699 --> 01:10:59,199
<b>The map says, in writing, that it was</b>

310
01:10:59,199 --> 01:11:00,500
<b>partially copied from</b>

311
01:11:00,500 --> 01:11:01,866
<b>a chart by Columbus.</b>

312
01:11:02,566 --> 01:11:03,733
<b>So what does the Piri</b>

313
01:11:03,733 --> 01:11:05,333
<b>Reis map actually say?</b>

314
01:11:05,833 --> 01:11:06,766
<b>It tells you where</b>

315
01:11:06,766 --> 01:11:08,333
<b>every line on it came from,</b>

316
01:11:08,800 --> 01:11:11,133
<b>and what every piece of land really is,</b>

317
01:11:11,766 --> 01:11:13,199
<b>Piri Reis wrote it down</b>

318
01:11:13,199 --> 01:11:16,399
<b>himself in 1513 on the parchment.</b>

319
01:11:16,800 --> 01:11:18,166
<b>We just didn't read it.</b>

